I'm still making progress through the Nethack classes and ascended K
the Knight to the status of demigodhood.

But, starting at the beginning,
I found an early magic lamp and a level 3 altar.  I got so excited
about having the Eye of the Aethiopica that I counted on doing a self-
conversion.  What I did not know at the time was that my only neutral
altar in the game might have been on the quest level.  Fortunately
there was a neutral altar available in the main dungeon.  What I did
not count on was how many turns it would take to generate a white
unicorn with which to perform the sacrifice.  Furthermore, I wanted to
wield Grayswandir.

What followed was approximately 70k turns of sacrificing, which
yielded:
Cleaver (beetle death drop!) Snickersnee, Demonbane, Firebrand,
Sunsword and finally Grayswandir!  Once suitably equipped I proceeded
to finish the quest.  I figured, hey! the quest monster is the imp so
how unlikely is it that I won't acquire teleport control from a
tengu?!  Eventually I ran out of food and patience and after killing
countless quasits and 28 tengu, I still did not have TC.  So let that
be a lesson for all of you reverse-genocide tengu folk out there!  You
just don't know what is going to happen.  Apparently, despite the fact
that quasits were extinct, they are still capable of being generated
on the quest level.  So, the probability of generating tengu did not
increase even after I had killed off 255 quasits.

With the quest finished and Grayswandir in hand it was time to self-
convert.  Eventually create monster was forgotten and it was a random
monster generation on a different level that allowed me to self-
convert.  I had to carry the white unicorn corpse down 3 levels.

For most of the game I rode around on dragons jousting baddies.
Entertaining.  Being a knight I had hoped to ascend while riding a
mount... sadly, many many dragons died in the attempt.  Black, the
black Dragon was the first to go shortly into the ascension run, then
Yellow, and then several more on the planes.  The main problem was
that their owner never found any scrolls of Gold detection or crystal
balls and the planes took much longer than they should have.
Negligent of me but I just felt like pushing my luck a little bit.
Eventually things got too close with Death and fainting from lack of
food !  Yipes!  So, being almost out of food and having to eat corpses
on the Astral Plane I figured that it was time to find the altar and
ascend.  The effect of casting charm monster was significant on my
hunger status.

Perhaps I should have melee'd more on the planes but I was hoping the
pets would help me locate the portals.  On earth I found the portal by
process of elimination, on fire I found the portal with a wand of
secret door detection and casting light, on air I found the portal by
observation and on water I found the portal while wearing the
amulet.

For almost the entire ascension run I was burdened and that gave the
Wizard what seemed like an extra turn to mess with me when he chased
me down.  But I had just enough holy waters and blessed remove curse
scrolls to keep safe.  this was my first game fighting Archons!
They're tough!

In retrospect although finding that white unicorn was a painfully long
process, having the Eye was immensely helpful.  Without it, charm
monster, controlled teleports for the ascension run,  and magic
missile would have been much more taxing.

I probably should have used a wish for a crystal ball to navigate the
planes easier but it was at least educational.  I was impressed at how
the planes shredded my pets; it was a meat grinder.

